            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a rise in fortune, then the Sanskrit for prosperity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: उन्नतिः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उन्नतिः — unnatiḥ — \"advancement; a rise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि शिक्षा उत्तमा, तर्हि समाजस्य उन्नतिः भविष्यति। yadi śikṣā uttamā, tarhi samājasya unnatiḥ bhaviṣyati. If education is good, society will advance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उन्नतिः (unnatiḥ) is built on ut, \"up\", and the root √nam, \"to bend\"; MW gives un-nati \"rising, ascending\" and \"elevation, height\", and \"advancement\" is how modern Sanskrit uses it (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
